  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tarok Danish. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Danish Tarok (Grosstarock) is a three-player trick-taking game using a 78-card tarot deck (21 trumps, Fool, 4 suits of 14). Primary objective: win the last trick with the Pagat (lowest trump) or a King. Secondary: win tricks and capture counting cards. Alliances form during play. Each player gets 25 cards (dealer gets 3 extra then discards to 25). Declarations at start: trump holdings, matadors (Fool, Pagat, 21), court combinations. Two pots (king pot, pagat pot). Card values: 4 for trump 21, Pagat, Fool, Kings; 3 Queens; 2 Knights; 1 Jacks. Closely related to German Grosstarock; survives mainly in Denmark.',
    objective: 'Primary: win the last trick with the lowest trump (trump 1) or a King. Secondary: win tricks and capture counting cards. Two pots (king pot, lowest-trump pot).',
    gameplay: 'Deal 25 cards each (dealer gets 3 extra then discards to 25). Declarations at start: trump holdings, matadors (Fool, lowest trump, 21), court combinations. Follow suit; must play trump if cannot follow. Card values: 4 for trump 21, lowest trump, Fool, Kings; 3 Queens; 2 Knights; 1 Jacks. Alliances form during play.',
